{
  "number": 1651,
  "title": "[BUG] guardrail_latest_message wrapping lost after tool execution (toolResult becomes last message)",
  "url": "https://github.com/strands-agents/harness-sdk/issues/1651",
  "state": "closed",
  "created_at": "2026-02-09T17:44:15Z",
  "closed_at": "2026-02-27T21:10:16Z",
  "body": "## Checks\n\n- [x] I have updated to the latest minor and patch version of Strands\n- [x] I have checked the documentation and this is not expected behavior\n- [x] I have searched [./issues](./issues?q=) and there are no duplicates of my issue\n\n## Strands Version\n\n1.24.0\n\n## Python Version\n\n3.13.9\n\n## Operating System\n\nmacOS 15.7.3 (Darwin 24.6.0, arm64)\n\n## Installation Method\n\npip\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\nWhen `guardrail_latest_message=True` is set on `BedrockModel`, the SDK wraps the latest user message in `guardContent` blocks so Bedrock only evaluates that message against the guardrail input policy. However, after a tool execution cycle, the last message in the conversation is a `toolResult` (role=user), not a text message. Because `toolResult` content doesn't match the `\"text\" in formatted_content or \"image\" in formatted_content` check in `_format_bedrock_messages()`, **no `guardContent` wrapping is applied to ANY message**.\n\nWithout any `guardContent` blocks in the request, Bedrock falls back to evaluating ALL user messages against the guardrail — including prior messages and tool results that contain domain-specific text (e.g., raw knowledge base passages). This causes spurious guardrail interventions on innocuous content.\n\n### Minimal reproduction\n\n```python\nfrom strands import Agent\nfrom strands.models import BedrockModel\n\n# 1. Create a Bedrock guardrail with a topic policy (e.g., blocking tax advice)\n# 2. Create agent with guardrail_latest_message=True and a tool that returns domain text\nmodel = BedrockModel(\n    model_id=\"us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\",\n    region_name=\"us-east-1\",\n    guardrail_id=\"<your-guardrail-id>\",\n    guardrail_version=\"1\",\n    guardrail_latest_message=True,\n)\nagent = Agent(model=model, tools=[your_knowledge_base_tool])\n\n# Turn 1: works — model uses tool, guardContent wraps the user text on first API call.\n# BUT on the second API call (after tool result), guardContent is lost.\nresult = agent(\"what is the standard deduction?\")\n# -> guardrail_intervened (false positive from tool result content)\n```\n\n### What happens internally\n\nMonkey-patching `_format_bedrock_messages` reveals the issue:\n\n```\nAPI Call #3 (first call of turn): 5 messages\n  [0] user: PLAIN_TEXT(\"hi\")\n  [2] user: PLAIN_TEXT(\"[User input redacted.]\")\n  [4] user: GUARD_CONTENT(\"what is the standard deduction?\")  ✅ wrapped\n\nAPI Call #4 (after tool execution): 7 messages\n  [0] user: PLAIN_TEXT(\"hi\")\n  [2] user: PLAIN_TEXT(\"[User input redacted.]\")\n  [4] user: PLAIN_TEXT(\"what is the standard deduction?\")  ❌ no longer wrapped!\n  [6] user: TOOL_RESULT  ← this is idx == len-1, but has no \"text\" key\n```\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nWhen `guardrail_latest_message=True`, the SDK should wrap the **last user message that contains text or image content** in `guardContent` blocks — not just the absolute last message. This ensures `guardContent` wrapping is maintained across multi-turn tool execution cycles within a single agent invocation.\n\n## Actual Behavior\n\nAfter tool execution, the last message is a `toolResult` (role=user). The condition at `bedrock.py` line 414 (`idx == len(messages) - 1`) only matches this `toolResult` message, which has no `text`/`image` content, so no `guardContent` wrapping is applied. The guardrail then evaluates ALL user messages, causing false positives from tool result content.\n\n## Additional Context\n\nThe bug is in `_format_bedrock_messages()`, lines 411-421:\n\n```python\nif (\n    guardrail_latest_message\n    and idx == len(messages) - 1        # <-- only checks absolute last\n    and message[\"role\"] == \"user\"\n    and (\"text\" in formatted_content or \"image\" in formatted_content)\n):\n```\n\nThis condition is only `True` for the final message in the list. After tool use, the message list ends with:\n\n```\n[N-2] user: \"question text\"          <- should get guardContent\n[N-1] assistant: toolUse(...)\n[N]   user: toolResult(...)          <- idx == len-1, but no \"text\" key\n```\n\nNeither message gets wrapped, so the entire request has no `guardContent` blocks.\n\n## Possible Solution\n\nPre-compute the index of the last user text/image message before the formatting loop:\n\n```python\nlast_user_text_idx = None\nif guardrail_latest_message:\n    for idx in range(len(messages) - 1, -1, -1):\n        msg = messages[idx]\n        if msg[\"role\"] == \"user\" and any(\n            \"text\" in cb or \"image\" in cb for cb in msg.get(\"content\", [])\n        ):\n            last_user_text_idx = idx\n            break\n\n# Then in the loop, replace the condition with:\n#   idx == last_user_text_idx\n```\n\n### Workaround\n\nApply the guardrail manually using the standalone `ApplyGuardrail` API on user input BEFORE sending it to the agent, and don't pass `guardrail_id`/`guardrail_version` to `BedrockModel`:\n\n```python\nimport boto3\n\ndef check_guardrail(message, guardrail_id, guardrail_version=\"1\"):\n    client = boto3.client(\"bedrock-runtime\")\n    response = client.apply_guardrail(\n        guardrailIdentifier=guardrail_id,\n        guardrailVersion=guardrail_version,\n        source=\"INPUT\",\n        content=[{\"text\": {\"text\": message}}],\n    )\n    return response.get(\"action\") == \"GUARDRAIL_INTERVENED\"\n\n# Check BEFORE calling agent\nif check_guardrail(user_input, guardrail_id):\n    print(\"Blocked by guardrail\")\nelse:\n    agent(user_input)\n```",
